$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of benzylchloroformate (1.0 equiv) and Amberlyst-15 (20
mg/mmol) was stirred for 5 min and amine (1.0 equiv) was added into it.
After stirring for the specified time (Table 1) at rt, the reaction
mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate and filtered through ordinary
filter paper. The catalyst was washed thoroughly with ethyl acetate and
the filtrate was concentrated. The resulting crude was purified by column
chromatography to get the pure N-benzyloxycarbonyl derivative. Table 3.
Cbz protection of amines via Scheme 1a Entry 1 89% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry (environmentally friendly process),
green chemistry-catalyst, green chemistry-solvent, Amberlyst in H+ form
used, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Amberlyst-15-catalyzed Cbz protection of amines under solvent-free
conditions
