$DATUM (3-Iodopropyl)[4-(methoxymethoxy)phenyl]carbamic Acid Methyl Ester (30b).
i-Pr2NEt (0.52 mL, 3.0 mmol) was added to a stirred and cooled (-35 °C)
solution of 30a (639.3 mg, 2.0 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (6 mL). MeOCOCl (0.23 mL,
3.0 mmol) was then added at a fast dropwise rate, and stirring was
continued for 40 min. The mixture was quenched with water and extracted
with EtOAc. The combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried
(MgSO4) and evaporated. Flash chromatography of the residue over silica,
using 1:5 EtOAchexane, gave 30b (700.9 mg) as a yellow oil:
(3-Iodopropyl)[4-(methoxymethoxy)phenyl]carbamic Acid Methyl Ester (30b),
yield 93% FTIR (neat) 2953, 1704, 1608, 1586, 1511 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3,
300 MHz) δ 2.11 (quintet, J = 7.1 Hz, 2 H), 3.14 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 2 H),
3.48 (s, 3 H), 3.68 (s, 3 H), 3.77 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 2 H), 5.17 (s, 2 H),
7.01-7.09 (m, 4 H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 1.9 (t), 32.3 (t), 51.3
(t), 52.9 (q), 56.1 (q), 94.5 (t), 116.7 (d), 128.3 (d), 135.4 (s), 155.9
(s), 156.3 (s); exact mass m/z calcd for C13H18INO4 379.02805, found
379.02831.
