$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Allyl 2-iodo-4,6-dimethylphenylcarbamate (S8): To a stirred solution of
aniline S1 (0.988 g, 4.00 mmol) in pyridine (10 mL) at 0 °C was added
allyl chloroformate (1.45 g, 12.0 mmol) dropwise via syringe over 5 min.
The mixture was warmed to room temperature, stirred overnight (16 h), and
poured into water (40 mL). The mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 40
mL), and the combined organic layers were washed sequentially with water,
sat. CuSO4 solution, 0.20 M HCl, and brine (40 mL each), dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated by rotary evaporation. Flash
chromatography (6:1 hexanes:EtOAc) afforded the title compound (1.23 g,
93%) as a cream-colored solid, Allyl 2-iodo-4,6-dimethylphenylcarbamate
(S8), yield 1.23 g, 93% mp 77-78 °C: 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.53 (s,
1H), 7.03 (s, 1H), 6.28-5.79 (m, 2H), 5.50-5.15 (m, 2H), 4.68 (br s, 2H),
2.31 (s, 3H), 2.28 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.8, 138.9,
137.2, 137.0, 134.1, 132.5, 131.6, 117.7, 99.8, 65.9, 20.3, 19.3; FTIR
(thin film, CHCl3, cm-1) 3270 (broad), 2921, 1707, 1508, 1232, 1056, 994,
936, 847, 771; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C12H14INNaO2 [M + Na]+: 353.9967,
found: 353.9964.
