$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S,S)-Methyl N,N-bis(1-phenylethyl)carbamate [(S,S)-9]: Phosgene (2.94
mL, 4.70 mmol,1.6 M solution in toluene) was added dropwise to a stirred
solution of (S,S)-bis(1- phenylethyl)amine [(S,S)-8, ee 99%]6 (0.962 g,
4.27 mmol) in dry toluene (20 mL) containing dry ethyldiisopropylamine (3
mL) at 0 °C under argon. After 30 min DMAP (0.132 g, 1.0 mmol) and dry
methanol (1 mL) were added and the reaction mixture was stirred for 16 h
at 70 °C. Water (30 mL) and conc. HCl (3 mL) were added to the cold
mixture. The phases were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted
with toluene (20 mL). The combined organic phases were washed with water
(30 mL) containing conc. HCl (3 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated
under reduce pressure. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
(hexanes/EtOAc 20:1; for TLC 10:1, R f = 0.31) to afford the carbamate
(S,S)-9 (1.121 g, 93%) as a colourless oil; [α]D 20 -131.7 (c 2.45,
acetone). IR (Si): 2977, 1690, 1446, 1275 cm-1; 1H NMR (400.13 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.22-6.98 (m, 6H), 7.02 (br. s, 4H), 5.01 (br. s, 2H), 3.56 (s,
3H), 1.67 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (100.61 MHz, CDCl3): δ 156.4,
141.4, 127.8, 127.6, 126.9, 53.1, 51.9, 18.2. Anal. Calcd for C18H21NO2:
C, 76.29; H, 7.47; N 4.94; Found: C, 76.08; H, 7.36; N, 4.92.
