$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Ketocarbamates 1. In a drybox,
imine (0.48 mmol) and chloroformate (1.91 mmol) were dissolved in
acetonitrile (10 mL) then the solution was stirred for 15 min in a 50 mL
reaction bomb. To this solution was added Pd2dba3•CHCl3 (25 mg, 0.024
mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 30 min until the Pd2dba3•CHCl3 was
dissolved. Tetrabutylammonium bromide (186 mg, 0.576 mmol) in methylene
chloride (5 mL) and the organostannane (0.53 mmol) in methylene chloride
(5 mL) were added to the reaction mixture. The solution was frozen in
liquid nitrogen then degassed, and carbon monoxide (15 psi) was added.
The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 24 h. After the reaction
period was completed, solvents were removed in vacuo. The product was
dissolved in 50 mL of ethyl acetate, then 25 mL of saturated KF solution
was added and the mixture was stirred for 5 h. This solution was filtered
over celite and extracted with ethyl acetate (3 X 50 mL). The organic
layers were combined and dried over MgSO4 then solvent was evaporated
under reduced pressure and the product was purified by silica gel
chromatography with hexane:ethylacetate as eluent.
Benzyl-(2-oxo-2-phenyl-1-p-tolyl-ethyl)-carbamic acid benzyl ester (entry
1) Yield: 93% 1HNMR (400MHz, CDCl3, 60 °C): δ 7.8 (s, br, 2H), 7.47-7.43
(t, 1H), 7.34-7.27 (t, 2H), 7.27-7.25 (m, 3H), 7.18-7.15 (m, 4H),
7.13-7.11 (m, 4H), 7.04-7.02 (d, 2H), 6.92 (s, br, 2H), 5.25-5.16 (dd,
2H), 4.95-4.91 (d, 1H), 4.33-4.29 (d, 1H), 2.27 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125MHz,
CDCl3, 60 °C): δ 197.6, 157.6, 139.4, 138.9, 136.5, 135.8, 133.3, 131.1,
130.7, 129.9, 129.0, 128.7, 128.6, 128.4, 128.1, 128.0, 127.3, 126.6,
67.9, 65.9, 49.0, 21.3. IR (KBr): νCO: 1703 cm-1, 1698 cm-1 HRMS.
Calculated for C30H28NO3+: 450.2069 found: 450.2063
