$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
aromatic Alloc-, CBz-, Troc-carbamates To a solution of sodium azide
(0.110 g, 1.70 mmol), sodium tert-butoxide (14.4 mg, 0.150 mmol), and
carboxylic acid (1.00 mmol) in DME (10.0 mL) at 25 °C, was added the
chloroformate reagent (1.10mmol) (Allylchloroformate: 120 μL,
benzylchloroformate: 150 μL, or 2,2,2 trichloroethylchloroformate:112
μL). Then the resulting mixture was stirred at 75 °C (85 °C for Troc
derivatives). When the reaction is completed by GC analysis, the mixture
was diluted with dichloromethane and a preabsorptionon silica was made.
The crude carbamate was then purified by flash chromatography onsilica
gel. Benzyl 2-iodophenylcarbamate (25). The title compound was prepared
from 2-iodobenzoic acid (248mg, 1.00 mmol) according to the general
procedure. The desired carbamate 25 (328 mg, 93%) was obtained as a white
solid, after flash chromatography (20% EtOAc/hexanes). Rf 0.57
(20%EtOAc/hexanes); mp 49 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.10 (d, J = 8
Hz, 1H), 7.77 (d, J = 8 Hz,1H), 7.46-7.33 (m, 6H), 7.05 (s (br), 1H),
6.81 (t, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 5.24 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,CDCl3) δ 153.2,
151.4, 138.8, 138.2, 135.7, 129.2, 128.6, 128.3, 125.1, 120.3, 88.8,
67.2; IR 3383,3031, 2953, 1732, 1586, 1514, 1432, 1201, 1036, 741 cm-1;
HMRS (ESI) calcd for C14H12INO2[M+H]+: 353.9985. Found: 353.9982.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement of aromatic carboxylic acids to access protected
anilines and aromatic ureas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lebel, Helene; Leogane, Olivier
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(25), 5717-5720

