$DATUM 5-Acetyl-5,6-dihydro-4H-benzo[f][1,2,3]triazolo[1,5-a][1,4]diazepine-6-carbonitrile
(45{1}). Acetyl chloride (20{1}) (37 mg, 34 µL, 0.47 mmol) was added to a
solution of amine 44 (50 mg, 0.24 mmol) and pyridine (56 mg, 57 µL, 0.71
mmol) in anhydrous MeCN (1.25 mL) at 0 ˚C, and the reaction was stirred
at room temperature for 3 h. The reaction was diluted with CH2Cl2 (20 mL)
and the mixture was washed with aqueous HCl (10 mL, 1.0 M) and saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (10 mL). The organic layer was dried (MgSO4) and
concentrated under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified by
flash chromatography eluting with EtOAc/toluene (6 : 4 → 7 : 3). 55 mg of
amide 45{1} (92 %) as a cream colored solid. mp 196-197 ˚C (colorless
needles from toluene); 1H NMR (500 MHz, d6-DMSO, 120 ˚C) δ 8.00 (dd, J =
7.6, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.00 (s, 1H), 7.83 (dd, J = 7.6, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.79 (app
td, J = 7.6, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.63 (app td, J = 7.6, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.74 (s,
1H), 5.38 (d, J = 15.0 Hz, 1H), 4.28 (d, J = 15.0 Hz, 1H), 2.28 (s, 3 H);
13C NMR (125 Mz, d6-DMSO, 120 ˚C) δ 168.6, 134.6, 132.6, 131.4, 131.3,
130.9, 129.3, 123.8, 123.0, 115.6, 47.4, 38.5, 20.7; IR (neat) 2926,
1667, 1661, 1499, 1395, 1233 cm-1 ; mass spectrum (CI) m/z 254.1044
[C13H12N5O (M+1) requires 254.1042], 227.
