$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis and spectroscopical data of benzyl
(3-{[(allylamino)carbonyl]amino}-2-benzylpropyl)carbamate (13) To a
solution of compound (R)-(-)-10m (116 mg, 0.47 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (6.0
mL) pyridine (56 μL, 0.56 mmol) and benzyl chloroformate (79 mL, 0.56
mmol) were successively added under nitrogen atmosphere. The mixture was
stirred for 4 h at room temperature and after this time the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure obtaining a reaction crude that was
purified by flash chromatography (20% EtOAc/hexane), affording 165 mg of
the biscarbamate (S)-(-)-13 as a colourless oil (92%). (S)-Benzyl
(3-{[(allylamino)carbonyl]amino}-2-benzylpropyl)carbamate (13). . Rf (20%
EtOAc/hexane): 0.23; IR (NaCl): ν 3325, 1555, 1522, 1245 cm-1; 1H-NMR
(CDCl3, 400.13 MHz): δ 2.00-2.04 (m, 1H), 2.56 (d, 3JHH = 5.3 Hz, 2H),
3.00-3.33 (m, 4H), 3.90-3.99 (m, 1H), 4.58 (d, 3JHH = 5.3 Hz, 2H),
5.07-5.19 (AB system, 2JHH = 12.2 Hz, 2H), 5.29-5.34 (m, 2H), 5.47-5.58
(brs, 2H), 5.88-5.97 (m, 1H), 7.16-7.38 (m, 10H); 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100.6
MHz): δ 36.2 (CH2), 41.0-41.4 (CH+2CH2), 65.7 (CH2), 66.8 (CH2), 117.7
(CH2), 126.3-128.9 (10CH), 132.9 (CH), 136.5 (C), 139.4 (C), 157.1 (C),
