$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2-iodo-4,6-dimethylphenylcarbamate (S13): To a stirred solution of
aniline S1 (1.24 g, 5.00 mmol) in pyridine (10 mL) at 0 °C was added
methyl chloroformate (0.709 g, 7.5 mmol) dropwise via syringe over 5 min.
The solution was warmed to room temperature and stirred 9 h. The mixture
was recooled to 0 °C, a second portion of methyl chloroformate (0.709 g,
7.5 mmol) was added in the same manner, and the mixture was stirred at
room temperature overnight (15 h). A final portion of methyl
chloroformate (0.709 g, 7.5 mmol) was again added at 0 °C, the mixture
was stirred for 2 h at room temperature, and water (50 mL) was slowly
added. The mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 50 mL) and the combined
organic layers were washed sequentially with water, sat. CuSO4 solution,
0.20 M HCl, and brine (50 mL each), dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated with rotary evaporation. Flash chromatography (4:1
hexanes:EtOAc) afforded the title compound (1.40 g, 92%) as a white solid
Methyl 2-iodo-4,6-dimethylphenylcarbamate (S13), yield 1.40 g, 92% mp
91-92 °C in a 2.3:1 ratio of rotamers: 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.54 (s,
1H), 7.03 (s, 1H), 6.14 (br s, 1H,major), 5.95 (br s, 1H, minor), 3.79
(br s, 3H), 2.30 (s, 3H), 2.28 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 154.5,
138.6, 137.0, 136.8, 134.1, 131.4, 99.8, 52.5, 20.1, 19.1; FTIR (thin
film, CHCl3, cm-1) 3286 (broad), 2953, 2921, 1710, 1502, 1449, 1349,
1241, 1068, 851, 771; LRMS (EI) m/z 305 (M+, 28), 178 (100), 163 (62),
118 (27); HRMS (EI) calcd for C10H12INO2 [M]+: 304.9913, found: 304.9904.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Radical and Anionic Cyclizations of Axially Chiral Carbamates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Guthrie, David B.; Curran, Dennis P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2009), 11(1), 249-251

