$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Peptidyl Carbamates 5 or 6 To a stirred solution of
Fmoc-β-aminoalkoxycarbonyl chloride/carbonate (1 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (10
ml) at -10°C was added a CH2Cl2 solution of amino acid methyl ester (1.2
mmol) or free peptidyl carbamate ester (obtained by the deprotection of
Fmoc-group using 20% diethylamine in CH2Cl2 for 30 min) and pyridine
(0.16 ml, 2.0 mmol) and allowed to stir at room temperature for 30 min.
Upon completion of the reaction, the reaction mixture was washed with
dilute HCl (10 ml), water (10 ml), 10% aqueous sodium carbonate (10 ml),
water (2 9 10 ml) and brine (2 9 10 ml). It was dried over sodium
sulphate and concentrated under vacuum and purified by column
chromatography using ethyl acetate: hexane (3:7) as eluant.
Fmoc-Phec-Val-OMe (5d). Yield(%): 92. mp 90–92°C; Calculated mass [M]+
530.61; ES MS found [M + 1]+ 531.6. Rf (30% EtOAc/Hexane): 0.51;[α]24
D:-3.64 (c = 1%, CHCl3); 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 0.88 (d, 2H, J = 6.7 Hz), 1.84
(m, 1H), 2.13 (m, H), 2.81 (d, 2H, J = 5.6 Hz), 3.74 (s, 3H), 4.06-4.43
(m, 6H), 5.09 (d, 1H, J = 6.9 Hz), 5.29 (t, 1H, J = 13.9 Hz), 7.18-7.78
(m, 13H), 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 18.5, 32.1, 38.2, 47.3, 52.3, 54.8, 64.5,
66.8, 67.7, 120.0, 125.0, 127.1, 127.2, 127.7, 128.6, 129.2, 135.7,
141.3, 144.0, 155.6, 156.3, 172.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Peptidyl Carbamates: Efficient Synthesis Using N-Fmoc-β-aminoalkoxy
Carbonyl Chlorides/Active Pentachlorophenyl Carbonates as Monomeric
Building Blocks
