$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedures for Synthesis of Carbamates: Method B. Preparation of
carbamates 5b, 6b, 7b, S1, S4, 10b, 11b, 12b, 13b, 13c, 13f, 13g, 14b,
and 14g. To a stirred solution of aldehyde (2.10 mmol) in MeOH (10.5 mL)
was added at rt a 40% MeOH solution of MeNH2 (0.429 mL, 4.20 mmol). After
1 h at rt, NaBH4 (159 mg, 4.20 mmol) was added at 0°C and the mixture was
stirred at rt for 30 min. The reaction mixture was quenched with acetone
(20 mL) at 0°C and the new mixture was concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residual white solids were used for the next step without
purification. To a stirred solution of the residue in a mixture of 1:1:1
THF-acetone-H2O (10.0 mL) was added at 0°C ClCO2R (3.78 mmol) or FmocOSu
(1.28 g, 3.78 mmol, for 17g and S15). After 2 h at rt, saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 (10 mL) was added at 0°C and the mixture was extracted with EtOAc
(10 mL x 3). The extracts were washed with saturated aqueous NaCl (10
mL), dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel to afford
carbamates 5b, 6b, 7b, S1, S4, 10b, 11b, 12b, 13b, 13c, 13f, 13g, 14b,
and 14g. From 3-methoxybenzaldehyde. Isopropyl
3-methoxybenzyl(methyl)carbamate (5b) as a colorless syrup, yield 92%. Rf
= 0.34 (3:1 hexane-EtOAc); IR (neat, cm-1) 2980, 1698, 1602, 1490, 1457,
1400, 1262, 1234, 1151, 1113; 1H NMR (500 MHz, (CD3)2SO, 80°C, solvent
residual peak = 2.50) δ 1.21 (6H, d, J = 6.3 Hz), 2.80 (3H, s), 3.76 (3H,
s), 4.38 (2H, s), 4.84 (1H, sept, J = 6.3 Hz), 6.77-6.86 (3H, m), 7.26
(1H, dd, J = 7.8, 7.8 Hz); 13C NMR (125 MHz, 80°C, (CD3)2SO) δ 21.5,
33.4, 51.2, 54.7, 67.6, 112.3, 112.8, 119.1, 129.1, 139.2, 155.1, 159.2;
LRMS (EI) m/z (M)+ 237.1; HRMS (EI) m/z (M)+ calcd for C13H19NO3
237.1365, found 237.1361.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
