$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-nicotinoyl-5,6-dihydro-4H-benzo[f][1,2,3]triazolo[1,5-a][1,4]diazepine-6-carbonitrile
(45{10}). A mixture of amine 44 (110 mg, 0.52 mmol), nicotinoyl chloride
hydrochloride (20{10}) (185 mg, 1.0 mmol) and pyridine (164 mg, 168 µL,
2.1 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (3.0 mL) was stirred at room temperature
for 2 h. Saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added and the reaction was
stirred at room temperature for 20 min. The reaction was then diluted
with CH2Cl2 (30 mL) and washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (20 mL). The
organic layer was dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced pressure,
and the residue was purified by flash chromatography eluting with
dichloromethane/MeOH (24 : 1 → 19 : 1 ). 153 mg (92%) of amide 45{10} as
a colorless solid. mp 187-189 ˚C (colorless microcrystals from i-PrOH);
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) (rotamers) δ 8.88-8.76, (comp, 2 H), 8.09 (d, J =
8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.95 (app dt, J = 7.9, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.90-7.74 (comp, 2 H),
7.70-7.46 (comp, 2 H), 7.51 (dd, J = 7.9, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 6.49 (br s, 1H),
5.10 (br s, 1H), 4.34 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.0,
152.7, 148.4, 135.9, 135.5, 133.8, 132.9, 131.5, 130.6, 130.2, 129.2,
124.7, 124.1, 123.3, 115.1, 47.7, 40.9; IR (neat) 2941, 2361, 1651, 1589,
1501, 1391, 1326, 1238, 1102 cm-1 ; mass spectrum (CI) m/z 317.1154
[C17H13N6O (M+1) requires 317.1151]; LCMS purity 92%.
