$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl hydroxy(methyl)carbamate To a stirred suspension of
N-methylhydroxylamine hydrochloride (10.0 g, 120 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in THF
(200 mL) and H2O (20 mL) was added NaHCO3 (20.0 g, 240 mmol, 2.0 equiv)
and methylchloroformate (10.0 mL, 132 mmol, 1.1 equiv). The resulting
clear suspension was stirred overnight at room temperature, then diluted
with H2O (100 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 х 100 mL). The combined
organic extracts were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vacuo to yield
the title compound which was used without further purification. Colorless
oil, yield (11.6 g, 92%). IR (thin film) 3268, 2956, 1723, 1455, 1367,
1255, 1194, 1145, 1062, 1030, 974, 908, 869, 838, 741 cm-1; 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.17 (br s, 1H, OH), 3.76 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.21 (s, 3H,
NCH3); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.7, 53.4, 38.1; HRMS (ESI-TOF)
calculated for C3H8NO3 [M+H]+ m/z 106.0499, found 106.0501.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Direct α-Amination of Aldehydes via a Photoredox
Mechanism: A Strategy for Asymmetric Amine Fragment Coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cecere, Giuseppe; Konig, Christian M.; Alleva, Jennifer L.; MacMillan,
David W. C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(31), 11521-11524

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME145 STEP1
$RXN



