$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Unsymmetrical Ureas 6 A solution of compound 3 (0.7 mmol), THF (30 mL),
and amine 4 (0.7 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After adding another amine 4 (0.7 mmol) and DMAP (1.4
mmol) for unsymmetrical diaryl urea 6k and 6l, the mixture was refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared. After evaporation of the solvent, the
product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm,
elution solvent: EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). 1-Butyl-3-phenylurea (6b),
yield 91%. mp 123 °C (lit.6 126 °C). Rf = 0.38 (THF / n-hexane = 1:3,
v/v). IR (KBr): 3380, 3309, 3267, 3188, 3109, 3035, 2958, 2929, 2867,
1693, 1652, 1598, 1556, 1498, 1315, 1230, 748 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
DMSO-d6): δ 0.89 (t, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz), 1.27-1.41 (m, 4H), 3.05-3.11 (m,
2H), 6.07 (t, NH, J = 5.3 Hz, D2O exchangeable), 6.87 (t, 1H, J = 7.2
Hz), 7.20 (t, 2H, J = 8.4 Hz), 7.37 (d, 2H, J = 8.4 Hz), 8.3 (bs, NH, D2O
exchangeable). 13C NMR 75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 14.11, 19.99, 32.34, 39.15,
118.05, 121.34, 129.04, 141.06, 155.68. Elemental analysis calcd for
C11H16N2O: C, 68.72; H, 8.39; N, 14.57. Found: C, 68.74; H, 8.42; N,
14.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM CAS# 932-22-9 recovered (100%, reusable)
