N,N-diethyl-N'-alkyl/aryl/phenylpiperazinoureas 4-6 and 8-12 To a
solution of (0.7 mol) aryl/alkylamine/phenylpiperazine,
N,N-diethylcarbamyl chloride was added dropwise (Scheme 2) at room
temperature with continuous stirring. Progress of reaction was monitored
via TLC (Mukund et al., 2004). After completion of reaction the reaction
mixture was purified with hexane, then evaporated in vacuo and the
resultant solid residue was crystallized from an appropriate solvent to
afford the pure derivatives 4-6 and 8-12, respectively.
N,N-Diethyl-N'-phenylpiperazinourea 8 Recrystallized from hexane (Yield
91%). mp 251 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ; 7.21 (1H, t, J4,(3,5) = 7.2 Hz, H4),
7.10 (2H, d, J2,3 = 6,5 = 7.2 Hz, H2,6), 6.93 (2H, t, J3,(4,2) = 5,(4,6)
= 7.2 Hz, H3,5), 3.47 (8H, br.s, 4CH2), 2.32 (4H, br.s, 2CH2), 1.53 (6H,
br.s, 2CH3)-EI MS: m/z (rel. abund. %); 261 (M+, 16), 246 (35), 232 (21),
189 (29), 184 (35)-Anal.: Calcd for C15H23N3O: C, 68.93; H, 8.87; N,
16.08%. Found: C, 68.97; H, 8.94; N, 16.11%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Antidepressant activity of carbamates and urea derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Perveen, Shahnaz; Fatima, Nasreen; Khan, Muhammad Aitmaud; Dar, Ahsana;
Khan, Khalid M.; Afza, Nighat; Voelter, Wolfgang
