$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of the 4-Nitrophenyl Carbamate (1) 2-Nitroaniline (0.1 g,
7.24 x 10-4 mol) was dissolved in 10 mL of dry THF/ DCM (1:1 v/v), then
cooled to 0°C, and NEt3 (0.10 mL, 7.24 x 10-4 mol) was added. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 10 min, and then a solution of
4-nitrophenylchloroformate (0.146 g, 7.24 x 10-4 mol) in dry THF/ DCM
(1:1 v/v) (5 mL) was added dropwise in a period of 10 min. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 1 h at the same temperature and 1 h at room
temperature. Finally it was filtered off, washed with distilled water,
and dried under vacuum at 80°C to give compound 1d. Yield: 91%. Mp:
118-119°C. IR (KBr): 3350 (s, N-H), 1745 (s, C=O), 1485 (s, NO2), 1380
(s, NO2), 1290 (s, C-O) cm-1. Yield: 0.200 g (91%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel and efficient synthesis of
4-substituted-1,2,4-triazolidine-3,5-diones from anilines
