$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for substituted
benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl carbamate 4a-g and 5a-g. Substituted 2-amino
benzothiazole (3a-g) (0.1 mmol), was dissolved in a 80 ml of dry
dichloromethane containing pyridine (0.1 mmol). To this solution was
added ethyl chloroformate (for 4a-g) or phenyl chloroformate (0.1 mmol)
(for 5a-g) and the reaction mixture was refluxed for 6 h. The reaction
mixture was then diluted with dichloromethane (200 ml) and washed with
portion of 1 M sodium bicarbonate solution, followed by water and then
brine. The organic layer was collected and dried over sodium sulfate. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure to yield the product which was
recrystallized from toluene: methanol mixture. Compound: 5c, Yield: 90 %.
M.P. 210-212 °C; Rf (benzene : methanol): 0.75 IR (cm-1): ArCH(2965),
NH(3173), C═O (1758), C═N(1631), C-N(1250), C-O(1039); 1H NMR(DMSO-d6) δ
ppm: CONH proton at 12 δ ppm was found to be D2O exchangeable,
12(1H,s,CONH),7-8 (8H, m,ArCH), 2.75(q, 2H, J = 7.2) 1.20 (t, 3H, J =
6.1); MS (m/z): 298 (M+),205.26(M-93),178(M-120).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of substituted benzo[d]thiazol-2-ylcarbamates as potential
anticonvulsants
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
