$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Cyclopropyl-3,3-dimethyl-1-(1-phenylbut-3-yn-1-yl)urea. To a solution
of N-(1-phenylbut-3-yn-1-yl)cyclopropanamine (800 mg, 4.32 mmol) in
toluene (9 mL) in a sealed tube was added dimethylcarbamyl chloride (0.52
mL, 5.19 mmol) and Et3N (0.72 mL, 5.19 mmol). The tube was sealed and the
reaction was stirred at 110 °C for 84 h. Water (30 mL) was added and the
aqueous portion was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 20 mL). The organic
extracts were combined, washed with brine (30 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (50 % EtOAc/hexane)afforded compound. Yield: (997 mg, 90
%), a yellow oil. νmax/cm-1: 1626 (s), 1489 (s), 1451 (m), 1396 (s), 1349
(m), 1233 (m); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.44-7.40 (2H, m, 2 × Ar-H),
7.33-7.22 (3H, m, 3 × Ar-H), 4.94 (1H, dd, J = 7.5, 7.5 Hz, C5-H), 3.10
(1H, ddd, J = 17.0, 8.5, 2.5 Hz, C6-H2), 2.99-2.90 (7H, m, 1 × C6-H2 and
2 × C4-H3), 2.33 (1H, tt, J = 6.5, 4.0 Hz, C2-H), 1.98 (1H, dd, J = 2.5,
2.5 Hz, C8-H), 0.65-0.45 (3H, m, 3 × C1-H), 0.30 (1H, m, C1-H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 163.9 (C3), 140.6 (Ar-C), 128.3, 128.0, 127.5 (5 ×
Ar-CH), 82.1 (C7), 70.4 (C8), 61.6 (C5), 38.1 (C4), 28.8 (C2), 22.4 (C6),
8.3 (C1), 8.1 (C1); m/z (CI+) 72 ([C3H6NO]+, 80 %), 129 ([C6H13N2O]+, 100
%), 257 ([M+H]+, 20 %), 285 ([M+C2H5]+, 10 %); HRMS: (CI+) Calculated for
C16H21N2O: 257.1654. Found [M+H]+: 257.1658.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
