$DATUM (R)-(-)-α-Methoxy-α-(trifluoromethyl)phenylacetyl chloride (33.4 mg,
0.132 mmol) was added slowly to a solution of (S)-S14 (all material
obtained in previous step), DMAP (1.3 mg, 0.01 mmol), and Et3N (16.7 mg,
0.17 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.2 mL) at 0 °C. The resulting mixture was warmed
to room temperature overnight with stirring, diluted with ether (15 mL),
quenched with saturated NH4Cl (15 mL), and extracted with Et2O (3 × 30
mL). The combined organic fractions were dried (MgSO4), and concentrated.
The residue was chromatographed (CH2Cl2-hexanes = 1:1 → 5:1) to give a
11.1:1 mixture of (R,S)-S13 and (R,R)-S13 (46.2 mg, 90%) as a white
solid. (R,S)-S13, yield (46.2 mg, 90%) mp = 204 °C. TLC (CH2Cl2- hexanes
= 1:1): Rf = 0.23. IR (neat, cm–1): 3625, 2981, 2872, 1648, 1418, 1146.
HRMS calcd (found) for C28H28F3NO2 (M+): 467.2072 (467.2073). NMR
assignments for (R,S)-S13 and (R,R)-S13 were made from analysis of this
mixture. For (R,S)-S13: 1H NMR (Figure S27): δ 6.47-7.49 (m, 15 H), 4.19
(dd, J = 2.0, 11.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.05-4.12 (m, 1 H), 3.71 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 3
H), 3.68 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.96 (ddd, J = 1.6, 6.8, 12.8 Hz, 1 H),
2.33-2.43 (m, 1 H), 2.07 (dd, J = 10.6, 13.0 Hz, 1 H), 1.41-1.52 (m, 1
H), 0.96 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3 H). 13C{1H} NMR (Figure S28): δ 164.5, 146.3,
143.8, 132.7, 129.4, 128.7, 128.6, 127.1, 127.0, 126.7, 126.6, 126.2,
126.1, 125.2, 122.3, 84.7, 84.5, 59.9, 57.1, 55.0, 53.2, 41.6, 26.3,
10.0.
