$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
N,N-diethyl-N'-alkyl/aryl/phenylpiperazinoureas 4-6 and 8-12 To a
solution of (0.7 mol) aryl/alkylamine/phenylpiperazine,
N,N-diethylcarbamyl chloride was added dropwise (Scheme 2) at room
temperature with continuous stirring. Progress of reaction was monitored
via TLC (Mukund et al., 2004). After completion of reaction the reaction
mixture was purified with hexane, then evaporated in vacuo and the
resultant solid residue was crystallized from an appropriate solvent to
afford the pure derivatives 4-6 and 8-12, respectively.
N,N-Diethyl-N'-(2,6-dimethylphenyl)urea 12 Recrystallized from hexane
(Yield 90%). mp 357 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ; 8.30 (1H, br.s, NH), 7.03 (3H,
m, Ar-H), 3.29 (6H, s, 2CH3), 2.49 (4H, br.s, 2CH2), 2.22 (6H, br.s,
2CH3)-EI MS: m/z (rel. abund. %); 220 (M+, 37), 205 (28), 191 (47),), 148
(33), 147 (100), 116 (85)-Anal.: Calcd for C13H20N2O: C, 70.87; H, 9.15;
N, 12.72%. Found: C, 70.82; H, 9.19; N, 12.75%.
