$DATUM Then to a solution of the racemic amino amide 12k (29 mg, 0.12 mmol) in
dry CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL) under nitrogen atmosphere were successively added
pyridine (12 mL, 0.15 mmol) and allyl chloroformate (16 mL, 0.15 mmol).
The mixture was stirred for 4 h at room temperature and after this time
the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure obtaining a reaction
crude that was purified by flash chromatography (100% EtOAc) affording 35
mg of the amido carbamate 11k as a colourless oil (90%). allyl
[3-(acetylamino)-2-(1-naphthyl)propyl]carbamate. Rf (100% EtOAc): 0.24;
IR (NaCl): ν 3318, 2933, 1702, 1651, 1540, 1437, 1372, 1260 cm-1; 1H-NMR
(CDCl3, 300.13 MHz): δ 1.95 (s, 3H), 3.47-3.79 (m, 4H), 3.69-3.99 (m,
1H), 4.56 (d, 3JHH = 5.6 Hz, 2H), 5.19-5.30 (m, 3H), 5.85-5.93 (m, 1H),
6.12 (m, 1H), 7.28-7.56 (m, 4H), 7.78-8.13 (m, 3H); 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 75.5
MHz): δ 23.0 (CH3), 39.1 (CH2), 41.1 (CH2), 42.7 (CH), 65.6 (CH2), 117.6
(CH2), 122.8 (CH), 123.3 (CH), 125.2 (CH), 125.8 (CH), 126.4 (CH), 127.7
(CH), 128.9 (CH), 131.7 (C), 132.5 (CH), 134.0 (C), 135.9 (C), 156.8 (C),
170.8 (C); MS (ESI+, m/z): 327 [(M+ H)+, 100%]; HRMS (EI) calcd for
C19H22N2O3 (M+): 326.1630; found: 326.1631; [a]D 20 = + 2.8 (c = 1.0,
EtOH) for 13% ee.
