$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Symmetric Ureas 7 A mixture of THF (30 mL), compound 3 (0.7 mmol), and
amine 4 (1.4 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared (TLC
monitoring). After adding DMAP (1.4 mmol), the mixture was then refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared (TLC monitoring). After evaporating the
solvent, the product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography
(2.5 × 7-11 cm, EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). 1,3-Bis(4-chlorophenyl)urea
(7c), yield 90%. mp 304 °C (lit.17 303-305 °C). Rf = 0.32 (EtOAc /
n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr): 3295, 3166, 3091, 3074, 1631, 1590, 1559,
1490, 1396, 1298, 1280, 1235, 1101, 1083, 822, 775, 638, 507 cm-1. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 7.32 (d, 4H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.48 (t, 4H, J = 8.8 Hz),
8.84 (bs, NH2, D2O exchangeable). 13C NMR (75MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 120.29,
125.97, 129.08, 139.00, 152.80. Elemental analysis calcd. for
C13H10Cl2N2O: C, 55.54; H, 3.59; N, 9.96. Found: C, 55.57; H, 3.61; N,
9.98.
