$DATUM N-benzoyl-cadaverine (1):4 To 202 mg (1 mmol) N-BOC-cadaverine and 111 mg
(1.1 mmol) triethylamine in 10 ml dry dichloromethane, 140 mg (1 mmol) of
fresh distilled benzoyl chloride in 10 ml dry dichloromethane was added
slowly under icebath cooling and nitrogen. After addition, the reaction
mixture was stirred at r.t. for 2 hours. The resulting milky suspension
was cooled again with an ice bath and a portion of 1.14 g (10 mmol)
trifluoroacetic acid (50% in dichloromethane) was added slowly, followed
by 2 hours of stirring at room temperature. The solvent and excess
trifluoroacetic acid was removed under vacuum. Fresh dichloromethane was
added and the solution was washed with bicarbonate, brine and dried over
sodium sulfate. Removal of the solvent resulted in a yellow oil that was
purified by column chromatography (CH2Cl2/MeOH/10:1 with a few drops of
33% NH4OH). Yield 185 mg (90%). N-benzoyl-cadaverine (1), yield 185 mg
(90%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.73 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.41 (t, J=
7.2 1H), 7.34 (dd, J= 7.6, J= 7.2, 2H), 6.73 (s, 1H), 3.38 (q, J= 6.88
Hz, 2H), 2.62 (t, J= 6.72 Hz, 2H), 1.55 (m, 2H), 1.48-1.30 (m, 6H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 167.7, 134.9, 131.3, 128.5, 127.0, 42.0, 40.0,
33.3, 29.4, 24.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
