$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Benzyl benzoyl(vinyl)carbamate (5e): Benzoyl chloride (1.20 equiv) was
added to a stirred solution of benzyl vinylcarbamate (1.00 equiv),
triethylamine (4.00 equiv) and DMAP (0.12 equiv) in dichloromethane at
room temperature under atmosphere of argon. The reaction was stirred for
2.5 h. The resulting mixture was concentrated under reduced pressure and
isolated by silica gel column chromatography giving corresponding product
5e. Yield 90%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.69 (d, 2H, J = 7.2 Hz), 7.53
(t, 1H, J = 7.2 Hz), 7.38 (t, 2H, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.20-7.30 (m, 2H), 6.97
(d, 2H, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.88 (dd, 1H, J = 6.8, 9.2 Hz), 5.04 (s, 2H), 4.98
(d, 1H, J = 15.6), 4.78 (d, 1H, J = 9.2 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Enantioselective Synthesis of Cyclopropylamine Derivatives via
Ru(II)-Pheox-Catalyzed Direct Asymmetric Cyclopropanation of
Vinylcarbamates
