$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedures for Synthesis of Carbamates: Method A. Preparation of
carbamates 1a, 1b, 1c, 1d, 1f, 9b, and 15b. To a stirred solution of
amine (2.10 mmol) in a mixture of 1:1:1 THF-acetone-H2O (10.0 mL) was
added at 0°C ClCO2R (3.78 mmol). After 2 h at rt, saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 (10 mL) was added at 0°C and the mixture was extracted with EtOAc
(10 mL x 3). The extracts were washed with saturated aqueous NaCl (10
mL), dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel to afford
carbamates 1a, 1b, 1c, 1d, 1f, 9b, and 15b. From N-methylbenzylamine.
Methyl benzyl(methyl)carbamate (1a) as a colorless syrup, yield 90%. Rf =
0.44 (2:1 hexane-EtOAc); IR (neat, cm-1) 3030, 2955, 1705, 1484, 1454,
1394, 1222, 1146, 771, 701; 1H NMR (500 MHz, (CD3)2SO, 80°C, solvent
residual peak = 2.50) δ 2.81 (3H, s), 3.65 (3H, s), 4.43 (2H, s),
7.21-7.29 (3H, m), 7.32-7.37 (2H, m); 13C NMR (125 MHz, 80°C, (CD3)2SO) δ
33.4, 51.4, 51.9, 126.7, 126.9, 128.1, 137.4, 156.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Smooth Isoindolinone Formation from Isopropyl Carbamates via
Bischler-Napieralski-Type Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
