$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Phenyl 4,5-Dichloro-6-oxopyridazine-1(6H)-carboxylate (3) To
a solution of 1 (3 mmol) and Et3N (3.6 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (30 mL) was
added dropwise the appropriate phenyl chloroformate (2), and the mixture
was stirred for 10 min at 5 °C (Scheme 1). After evaporating the solvent,
the product was extracted with Et2O-H2O (7:2, v/v). The organic layer was
dried over anhyd MgSO4, and then evaporated under reduced pressure. The
resulting residue was recrystallized from THF-n-hexane (1:3, v/v) to give
the product 3. White powder, yield (0.78 g, 90%). Mp 140 °C. Rf = 0.77
(CH2Cl2). IR (KBr): 3074, 3043, 1793, 1681, 1602, 1483, 1272, 1188, 1070,
948, 877, 750, 617 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 7.33-7.41 (m, 3
H), 7.53 (t, 2 H, J = 7.2 Hz), 8.38 (s, 1 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6):
δ = 121.52, 127.51, 130.52, 135.42, 136.96, 138.34, 149.53, 150.58,
154.73. Anal. Calcd for C11H6Cl2N2O3: C, 46.34; H, 2.12; N, 9.83. Found:
C, 46.36; H, 2.15; N, 9.87.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phenyl 4,5-dichloro-6-oxopyridazine-1(6H)-carboxylate as carbonyl source:
facile and selective synthesis of carbamates and ureas under mild
conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
