$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure J: Synthesis of Carbamates
To a solution of amine (1 equiv) in THF/H2O (50:50, 0.25 M) cooled to 0
°C was added NaHCO3 (1.5 equiv) and the alkyl chloroformate (1.5 equiv).
The reaction mixture was stirred for 2 h at rt, then diluted with EtOAc
and sat NH4Cl. The organic layer was washed with sat. NaHCO3 and brine,
dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated. The resulting oil was
purified by column chromatography. isopropyl benzylcarbamate 13 Following
general procedure J, a mixture of N-benzylamine (2.18 mL, 20 mmol),
NaHCO3 (2.52 g, 30 mmol), and isopropyl chloroformate (3 mL, 30 mmol) was
stirred for 2 h at rt. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (10-80% EtOAc/hexanes) to provide the title compound as an
oil (3.4 g, 89%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.36– 7.26 (m, 5H),
4.96–4.88 (m, 2H), 4.37 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 2H), 1.24 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 6H).
