$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Unsymmetrical Ureas 6 A solution of compound 3 (0.7 mmol), THF (30 mL),
and amine 4 (0.7 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After adding another amine 4 (0.7 mmol) and DMAP (1.4
mmol) for unsymmetrical diaryl urea 6k and 6l, the mixture was refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared. After evaporation of the solvent, the
product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm,
elution solvent: EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v).
N-Phenylpiperidine-1-carboxamide (6c), yield 89%. mp 168 °C (lit.7 168
°C). Rf = 0.26 (EtOAc / n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr): 3286, 3128, 3054,
2940, 2934, 2874, 2854, 1628, 1597, 1535, 1448, 1415, 1302, 1029, 754
cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 1.44-1.60 (m, 6H), 3.37-3.42 (m, 4H),
6.90 (t, 1H, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.20 (t, 2H, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.44 (d, 2H, J = 7.5
Hz), 8.39 (bs, NH, D2O exchangeable). 13C NMR 75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 24.57,
25.97, 45.12, 120.03, 121.92, 128.66, 141.23, 155.36. Elemental analysis
calcd. for C12H16N2O: C, 70.56; H, 7.90; N, 13.71. Found: C, 70.58; H,
7.91; N, 13.72.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM CAS# 932-22-9 recovered (100%, reusable)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phenyl 4,5-dichloro-6-oxopyridazine-1(6H)-carboxylate as carbonyl source:
