$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Unsymmetrical Ureas 6 A solution of compound 3 (0.7 mmol), THF (30 mL),
and amine 4 (0.7 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After adding another amine 4 (0.7 mmol) and DMAP (1.4
mmol) for unsymmetrical diaryl urea 6k and 6l, the mixture was refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared. After evaporation of the solvent, the
product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm,
elution solvent: EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). 1-Butyl-3-p-tolylurea (6g),
yield 89%. mp 105 °C (lit.11 118 °C). Rf = 0.33 (EtOAc / n-hexane = 1:2,
v/v). IR (KBr): 3302, 2917, 1639, 1615, 1594, 1565, 1515, 1308, 1237,
813, 505 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 0.89 (t, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz),
1.23-1.44 (m, 4H), 2.2 (s, 3H), 3.02-3.09 (m, 2H), 6.02 (t, NH, J = 5.4
Hz, D2O exchangeable), 7.00 (d, 2H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.25 (d, 2H, J = 8.1
Hz), 8.23 (bs, NH, D2O exchangeable). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 14.15,
19.98, 20.73, 32.37, 39.13, 118.11, 129.45, 130.01, 138.49, 155.73.
Elemental analysis calcd. for C12H18N2O: C, 69.87; H, 8.80; N, 13.58.
Found: C, 69.89; H, 8.83; N, 13.61.
