$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Ureas 4 To a solution of 3 (1.10
g, 3.6 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (15 mL), amine (10 equiv), and 4-DMAP (10 equiv)
were added and the mixture was stirred in the dark overnight at r.t. It
was then washed with 3% HCl and 3% NaHCO3 solution, extracted with
CH2Cl2, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
crystallized from CHCl3 to get pure compound 4.
1-(Benzylcarbamoyl)-5-bromo-7-nitroindoline (4a) Synthesized from 3 and
benzylamine in 89% yield. mp 182-183 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 7.82 (m, 1
H), 7.46 (m, 1 H), 7.36-7.31 (m, 5 H), 5.02 (br s, 1 H, NH), 4.48 (d, J =
6.5 Hz, 2 H), 4.13 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 2 H), 3.24 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 2 H). 13C
NMR (CDCl3): δ = 161.3, 142.4, 142.2, 138.3, 131.7, 128.9, 127.9, 127.84,
125.8, 120.5, 50.58, 45, 28.8. HRMS: m/z calcd for C16H14BrN3O3:
375.0232; found: 375.023 [M]+ .
