$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of N-(1-cymantrenylethyl)amides
(general procedure). An appropriate acid chloride (15 mmol) was added at
-20 °C to a solution of 1-aminoethylcymantrene 12 (2.5 g, 10 mmol) and
Et3N (2.8 mL, 20 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (50 mL). The reaction mixture was warmed
to room temperature, stirred for an additional 2 h, neutralized with 10%
aqueous NH4Cl (50 mL), and stirred for 20 min. The organic layer was
separated, washed successively with 20% aqueous H3PO4, aqueous NaHCO3,
and water, and dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed and the residue
was crystallized from hexane. This procedure was used to obtain compounds
7-9. N-(1-Cymantrenylethyl)pivalamide (9). Yield 3.0 g (89%), m.p. 71-72
°C. 1H NMR (benzene-d6), δ: 1.07 (d, 3 H, CHMe, J = 6.6 Hz); 1.22 (s, 9
H, CMe3); 3.96 (m, 1 H, β-HCp); 3.97 (m, 1 H, β´-HCp); 4.28 (m, 1 H,
α-HCp); 4.44 (m, 1 H, α´-HCp); 5.01 (m, 1 H, CHMe); 5.52 (m, 1 H, NH). IR
(benzene), ν/cm-1: 2017 (CO), 1938 (2 CO), 1673 (C=O). UV (benzene),
λmax/nm (ε /mol-1cm-1): 339 (2089). Found (%): C, 54.33; H, 5.35; N,
4.12; Mn, 15.80. C15H18MnNO4. Calculated (%): C, 54.38; H, 5.44; N, 4.23;
Mn, 15.67.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Orientation in the metalation of amide, carbamate, ureido, and allylic
derivatives of cymantrene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
