$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Troc-Gly-Ot-Bu 15: Into a THF (10 mL, 0.50 M)
solution of tertbutylglycinate (683 uL, 5.0 mmol) and pyridine (610 μL,
7.5 mmol) was added trichloroethyl chloroformate (810 μL, 6.0 mol) slowly
at 0 °C. The reaction was warmed up to rt and stirred for 2 h. The
solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue was diluted with EtOAc. The
solution was washed with 0.2N HCl (2X), NaHCO3 (2X), brine (1X), dried
over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. Purification by chromatography on
silica gel (Hexane: EtOAc= 6: 1) afforded carbamate 15 as a colorless oil
(99% yield). 2,2,2-Trichloroethyl
2-methoxydibenzo[b,d]furan-3-ylcarbamate 21: Prepared according to the
procedure for 15 (89% yield) as a white powder after flash chromatography
on silica gel (hexane: CH2Cl2= 3: 1 to 0: 1). mp. 158-159°C; IR (thin
film) νmax: 3413, 2951, 1746, 1606, 1520, 1467, 1204, 1097, 1045, 972,
832, 750 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.41 (1H, br s), 7.84 (1H, d, J
= 7.6 Hz), 7.69 (1H, br s), 7.55 (1H, d, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.41 (1H, t, J =
7.6 Hz), 7.34 (1H, s), 7.32 (1H, t, J = 7.6 Hz), 4.90 (2H, s), 4.00 (3H,
s) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 156.8, 151.4, 151.0, 144.8, 126.9,
126.4, 124.6, 122.7, 120.0, 118.5, 111.8, 102.3, 102.2, 95.5, 74.8, 56.5
ppm; ESI-HRMS calcd. for C16H12Cl3NO4Na [M+Na]+: 409.1614, found
409.1587.
