$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of aromatic ureas.To a solution of
sodium azide (0.110 g, 1.70 mmol), sodium tert-butoxide (14.4 mg, 0.150
mmol), andcarboxylic acid (1.00 mmol) in DME (10.0 mL) at 25 °C, was
added the phenylchloroformate (140 μL,1.10 mmol). The resulting mixture
was stirred at room temperature for 8 hours. The amine derivative (1.50
mmol) was then added and the reaction mixture was stirred at for 16
hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature and diluted
with hexane (40 mL). The resulting solution is poured into ice-cold water
with continuous stirring, 10 mL water was added and the stirring
maintains during 20minutes. The solid was filtered and recrystallized
when needed. 1, 3-Diphenylurea (33). The title compound was prepared from
benzoic acid (122 mg, 1.00 mmol) andaniline (137 μL, 1.50 mmol) according
to the general procedure. The desired urea 33 (189 mg, 89%) was obtained
as a white solid after filtration. Rf 0.51 (40% EtOAc/hexanes); mp 219
°C; 1H NMR (400MHz, DMSO) δ 8.24 (s (br), 2H), 7.45 (d, J = 8 Hz, 4H),
7.27 (t, J = 8 Hz, 4H), 6.96 (t, J = 7 Hz, 2H);13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO) δ
152.4, 139.6, 128.7, 121.7, 118.1; IR 3281, 3036, 1646, 1592, 1538,1496,
1439, 1230, 893, 751 cm-1; HMRS (ESI) calcd for C13H12N2ONa [M+Na]+:
235.0842. Found: 235.0843.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement of aromatic carboxylic acids to access protected
anilines and aromatic ureas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lebel, Helene; Leogane, Olivier
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(25), 5717-5720

