$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The residue was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (3 mL). To this solution DMAP (25 mg,
0.211 mmol) was added followed by Et3N (1.7 mL, 12.6 mmol). The mixture
was cooled to 0 °C, and phenyl chloroformate (1 mL, 3.1 mmol) was added
neat. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature. After
15 min of being stirred, the reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc and
transferred into a separatory funnel. The reaction mixture was washed
with H2O, saturated aqueous NaHCO3, and brine. The organic layer was
dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated down. The solid residue was
washed with hexanes and filtered. 0.774 g (89%) of 17. No further
purification was necessary.
N-[1-(2,2-Dimethyl[1,3]dioxolan-4-yl)-2-(4-phenylpiperazine-1-yl)ethyl]benzamide
(17). Rf = 0.3 (30% EtOAc in hexanes); t R = 8.3 min (100%) (75-300 °C at
25 °C/min, 10 min); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.30-7.02 (m, 7H, Ph),
6.86-6.75 (m, 3H, Ph), 5.38 (d, J = 5 Hz, 1H, NH), 4.22-4.16 (m, 1H,
OCH), 4.03 (dd, J = 6, 8.7 Hz, 1H, OCHH), 3.92 (dd, J = 6, 8.7 Hz, 1H,
OCHH), 3.87-3.78 (m, 1H, NHCH), 3.13-3.10 (m, 4H, PhN(CH 2)2), 2.69-2.54
(m, 6H, N(CH 2)3), 1.38 (s, 3H, CH 3), 1.29 (s, 3H, CH 3); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ 154.8, 151.2, 150.9, 129.3, 129.1, 125.4, 121.6, 119.7,
116.0, 109.6, 76.8, 66.8, 57.7, 53.7, 51.2, 49.3, 29.7, 26.4, 25.1. HRMS:
calcd for C24H31N3O4 ·Na+, 448.2207; found, 448.2199.
