$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure D. The phenol (1.2 mmol) was
dissolved in 4 mL of aqueous 0.3 M NaOH and added to a 10 mL CH2Cl2
solution of CSCl2 (1.8 mmol). The two layers were stirred vigorously for
1 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed with brine.
The organic layer was dried with Na2SO4, and solvent and excess CSCl2
were removed under reduced pressure. The reaction mixture was then
redissolved in 10 mL of CH2Cl2. Neat N-methylaniline (2.4 mmol) was then
added to the above CH2Cl2 solution of the reaction mixture and stirred
for 10 min. The reaction was then diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed with
brine followed by 10 mL of 0.1 N HClaq. The organic layer was dried with
Na2SO4. Solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the crude mixture
was purified by column chromatography. The corresponding thiocarbamate.
O-(2-Naphthyl)-N-methyl-N-phenyl thiocarbamate (28): procedure D; white
solid; 88%. mp 129-131 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.78 (3H, m), 7.41
(5H, m), 7.31 (3H, m), 7.19 (1H, m), 3.74 (3H, s); 13C NMR(100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 188.06, 151.63, 143.58, 133.68, 131.55, 129.53, 129.04, 127.90,
127.81, 127.74, 126.54, 125.79, 125.71, 122.26, 119.35; HRMS (ESI+) calcd
for C18H15ONS 294.09526 [M+H]+, found 294.09548 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Radical O→C Transposition: A Metal-Free Process for Conversion of Phenols
into Benzoates and Benzamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
